WEBVTT

00:02.336 --> 00:03.803
Legend has it that...

00:04.838 --> 00:07.602
...during the Heian Period, there were
men who fought with no weapons.

00:08.108 --> 00:13.444
They were known as the Men of
Carnage and they reigned undefeated.

00:14.915 --> 00:20.080
Their technique was called
the Mutsu Enmei Style.

00:33.200 --> 00:40.629
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

00:40.908 --> 00:46.744
<i>Rushing through my innocent</i>
<i>youth without a care in the world.</i>

00:48.282 --> 00:54.187
<i>This soul of mine is</i>
<i>so easy to influence.</i>

00:55.856 --> 00:59.622
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

00:59.727 --> 01:02.924
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

01:06.700 --> 01:13.765
<i>This is what I'm wishing</i>
<i>for as I sing this song.</i>

01:13.941 --> 01:19.777
<i>I want you to acknowledge</i>
<i>me, that's all.</i>

01:20.647 --> 01:27.917
<i>You smiled at me for</i>
<i>the very first time.</i>

01:28.088 --> 01:36.496
<i>Thank you so much, thank you</i>
<i>from the bottom of my heart.</i>

01:37.197 --> 01:38.858
<i>I'll never forget it.</i>

01:48.609 --> 01:52.045
<i>Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

01:54.982 --> 02:00.181
<i>Going North</i>

02:30.784 --> 02:32.445
So the bastards are here, eh?

02:36.256 --> 02:43.253
August 1868, Toshizo
Hijikata is in combat in Aizu.

02:43.931 --> 02:44.920
Going north...

02:45.065 --> 02:45.399
<i>Tsuruga Castle</i>
<i> </i>

02:45.399 --> 02:46.600
<i>Tsuruga Castle</i>
Going north...

02:46.600 --> 02:47.067
<i>Tsuruga Castle</i>
<i> </i>

02:47.067 --> 02:48.534
<i>Tsuruga Castle</i>
A journey bringing them...

02:48.635 --> 02:51.627
...ever closer to the moment of defeat.

02:54.708 --> 02:56.039
Hijikata?

02:57.277 --> 03:00.075
Oh, it's you, Dr. Ryojun.

03:00.481 --> 03:01.948
What a surprise!

03:02.149 --> 03:05.482
I see you've cut off your topknot.
I thought you were someone else!

03:05.886 --> 03:10.220
Well, since we've switched
to Western combat techniques...

03:10.357 --> 03:11.324
Does it not suit me?

03:11.792 --> 03:13.657
No, it suits you very well.

03:14.061 --> 03:17.121
You're a good-looking man,
even in Western clothes!

03:17.564 --> 03:21.398
Anyway, the reason I'm here is
because I needed to speak with you.

03:23.470 --> 03:25.836
You see...

03:26.273 --> 03:28.741
I've put off telling
you this before, Hijikata...

03:28.842 --> 03:31.140
...since I didn't
want it to affect your morale...

03:31.411 --> 03:35.177
But the way the battle is going, there's
no telling if we'll ever meet again.

03:35.549 --> 03:36.607
So I decided...

03:36.750 --> 03:37.876
Oh, sorry.

03:38.118 --> 03:41.645
You're about to go into battle.
Forgive me for being morbid.

03:41.989 --> 03:44.457
That's quite all right.
It's true, after all.

03:44.925 --> 03:49.021
I had come here to ask for
reinforcements, and was turned down.

03:49.263 --> 03:50.127
So?

03:51.298 --> 03:55.564
At the end of May, Okita passed away.

03:57.304 --> 03:58.771
Is that right?

03:59.706 --> 04:02.300
I don't know the details
surrounding his death...

04:02.442 --> 04:06.105
...but that's what I was told in
a letter from my family back home.

04:06.647 --> 04:11.311
I see, so you are gone now, too,
Soushi?

04:14.288 --> 04:18.622
And now, there's no one left but me,
eh?

04:19.760 --> 04:23.218
"Please wait for me..."
That was his message to you...

04:23.430 --> 04:25.625
...but as I suspected,
he couldn't hold on.

04:26.967 --> 04:29.458
Wait for him, eh?

04:30.571 --> 04:35.406
It looks like Soushi's the one who'll
have to wait for me, in the next world.

04:35.809 --> 04:40.371
Hijikata, you mustn't do
anything to hasten your death!

04:41.081 --> 04:42.776
You don't need to worry about that.

04:43.050 --> 04:47.111
I didn't shed a tear, even when
you told me of Soushi's death.

04:47.654 --> 04:50.350
It was the same as when I heard
about Kondo's death...

04:50.457 --> 04:52.652
That's the kind of man I am.

04:53.560 --> 04:56.654
I'm not ready to die in a
mere skirmish at Bonari Pass.

04:56.797 --> 04:59.357
I shall continue to fight, on and on!

05:00.133 --> 05:01.828
Hijikata...

05:02.302 --> 05:05.567
You're a strong man, so strong.

05:06.640 --> 05:09.734
Nevertheless, the Bakufu
has already collapsed.

05:10.210 --> 05:12.508
It's just a matter of
time before Aizu falls.

05:12.813 --> 05:16.340
You say you're going to
keep fighting, but how far...

05:17.084 --> 05:18.745
How far do you plan to go?

05:20.020 --> 05:21.817
All the way to hell!

05:25.392 --> 05:29.886
Although if I go to hell, I
won't get to see you, Soushi...

05:42.175 --> 05:43.540
Hijikata!

05:44.111 --> 05:45.669
What is it, Saito?

05:45.779 --> 05:47.337
You're really pushing your luck!

05:47.447 --> 05:50.712
For god's sake, could you at
least try to hide a little?

05:51.051 --> 05:53.451
At this distance, and
the way they're shooting...

05:53.553 --> 05:55.282
...there's no way
they're going to hit us!

06:06.800 --> 06:08.199
Now's the time...

06:08.602 --> 06:09.534
Special Attack Unit!

06:09.903 --> 06:11.700
Charge!

06:15.509 --> 06:19.104
Hijikata... it won't take long
for that unit to get through.

06:19.279 --> 06:21.213
Well, they outnumber us by far.

06:21.481 --> 06:25.212
It looks like our own
riflemen have retreated.

06:26.253 --> 06:27.277
Let's go, Saito!

06:27.421 --> 06:28.251
Right!

06:30.691 --> 06:31.521
Come on, men!

06:31.625 --> 06:32.819
Right!

06:33.026 --> 06:36.359
Shinsengumi! Charge!

06:42.803 --> 06:44.464
It's the Shinsengumi!

06:46.640 --> 06:49.507
You're outnumbered, are you mad?

06:50.343 --> 06:52.174
More than you, at least!

06:56.416 --> 06:59.214
It's the Shinsengumi! All right, then...

06:59.519 --> 07:00.486
Riflemen!

07:06.993 --> 07:10.429
It will be quite a coup for
you if you can take my head.

07:11.832 --> 07:15.563
I am the Deputy Commander of
the Shinsengumi, Toshizo Hijikata!

07:16.970 --> 07:19.564
Hijikata, the Demon of Kyoto?

07:42.462 --> 07:44.225
Infiltrate the enemy lines, men!

07:45.532 --> 07:47.523
At close range, their rifles won't...

07:49.302 --> 07:50.735
The stronghold!

07:58.445 --> 08:00.310
They're holding them off well.

08:01.348 --> 08:05.148
I'll bet Hijikata's
in command over there.

08:05.819 --> 08:08.151
I've caught up with you at last!

08:10.223 --> 08:13.021
Still, there's no time to lose.

08:13.727 --> 08:16.161
Defending that pass puts
them at a disadvantage.

08:16.363 --> 08:19.662
Not only that, but there are far too
many Imperial troops on the attack.

08:20.567 --> 08:23.434
No matter how fierce a fight he puts
up, Hijikata doesn't stand a chance...

08:24.504 --> 08:25.698
That's where we stand.

08:25.806 --> 08:27.603
You stay here and wait for me.

08:27.741 --> 08:29.538
I'm going to go see Hijikata.

08:30.710 --> 08:32.109
No!

08:34.114 --> 08:35.411
I'm not going to let you escape!

08:37.517 --> 08:39.280
Hey, I'm not going to escape.

08:39.386 --> 08:43.584
If I really wanted to get away,
why would I let you keep up with me?

08:44.825 --> 08:48.761
Even so, I never thought
you'd hang on this long.

09:44.851 --> 09:47.081
For more than two months now...

09:47.220 --> 09:51.088
...you've followed me all the
way, still carrying Okita's sword.

09:55.662 --> 09:57.653
How long are you
planning to keep this up?

09:58.231 --> 10:00.495
Until I've avenged Lord Okita's death.

10:00.934 --> 10:04.267
Until I've killed you
with Lord Okita's sword!

10:04.838 --> 10:07.204
You'll never be able
to kill me, you know.

10:07.874 --> 10:09.466
I know that!

10:10.477 --> 10:15.779
But I'll keep staying close to you. You
have to let your guard down eventually.

10:15.916 --> 10:17.178
That's when I'll make my move.

10:19.085 --> 10:22.384
That Okita must've had some hold on
you...

10:22.756 --> 10:24.519
You may be right.

10:25.225 --> 10:28.023
Fine, follow me as much as you want.

10:29.162 --> 10:33.531
And now, you've followed
me all the way to Aizu!

10:34.634 --> 10:36.898
What's so funny?

10:38.238 --> 10:41.435
If I wanted to flee, I'd have
done so long ago, that's all.

10:43.143 --> 10:45.577
So you wait here, got that?

10:46.212 --> 10:48.840
You shouldn't get any
closer to the battlefield...

10:52.185 --> 10:55.177
Even so! There's no guarantee
that you'll come back!

10:58.325 --> 10:59.792
I give you that.

11:00.060 --> 11:03.461
But if I survive, I swear
to you that I'll return.

11:03.630 --> 11:04.790
Wait for me!

11:05.298 --> 11:06.788
Stop! You murderer!

11:12.739 --> 11:16.072
What do you mean, "if I survive"?

11:18.244 --> 11:22.180
I'm going to avenge Lord Okita
if it's the last thing I do!

11:22.315 --> 11:23.009
I won't let him...

11:30.690 --> 11:31.714
He's gone!

11:32.225 --> 11:33.453
Where'd he go?

11:41.701 --> 11:44.499
Oh, no! I must save his
sword, if nothing else!

11:44.604 --> 11:45.593
I'm going to fall!

11:53.680 --> 11:55.011
I-I stopped falling!

11:55.715 --> 11:56.704
But...

11:58.218 --> 11:59.981
Idiot! Let go of that
sword for god's sake...

12:00.186 --> 12:02.848
...just toss it and
hang on with both hands!

12:02.956 --> 12:04.514
Or else you're going to fall!

12:05.392 --> 12:06.484
I won't do it!

12:06.693 --> 12:10.220
If it means I have to throw away
Lord Soushi's sword, then let me fall!

12:10.997 --> 12:13.192
Lord Soushi, I'll be with you soon...

12:20.507 --> 12:21.735
Goddammit!

12:22.776 --> 12:24.107
You moron!

12:24.377 --> 12:27.938
That's nothing but a
sword, it's not Okita.

12:30.817 --> 12:32.409
Who asked you for help?

12:34.154 --> 12:35.382
Oh, the hell with it...

12:39.759 --> 12:42.660
Listen! You hang on to that sword now!

12:57.644 --> 12:59.168
I'm saved...

13:06.920 --> 13:08.148
He's gone...

13:10.190 --> 13:13.125
He must have fallen...

13:14.794 --> 13:16.227
But why?

13:35.849 --> 13:36.713
Hey!

13:37.484 --> 13:40.544
Idiot! You planning to
spend the night down there?

13:43.256 --> 13:44.188
Come on up!

13:45.992 --> 13:47.653
Y-You're alive!

13:48.261 --> 13:49.319
What's this?

13:49.429 --> 13:50.896
Have you been crying?

13:51.030 --> 13:52.827
I'm your enemy, remember?

13:59.539 --> 14:00.801
What's going on?

14:01.074 --> 14:03.133
Look, I think you've got the wrong
idea...

14:03.376 --> 14:08.211
You don't think I'd actually give up
my own life just to save you, do you?

14:08.348 --> 14:10.077
I hope not!

14:10.183 --> 14:11.047
What?

14:11.417 --> 14:13.942
You think a fall like
that would kill me?

14:14.320 --> 14:16.550
I did it because I was
sure we'd both make it.

14:18.825 --> 14:21.157
Come on! Can you walk?

14:23.029 --> 14:23.927
Ouch...

14:24.164 --> 14:25.631
It's your ankle, huh?

14:25.732 --> 14:27.063
Looks pretty bad.

14:27.333 --> 14:28.357
All right!

14:33.740 --> 14:34.900
Your arm...

14:35.808 --> 14:37.969
That's right, it's broken.

14:38.378 --> 14:40.812
I messed up my landing a little.

14:40.980 --> 14:42.379
That's all.

14:44.250 --> 14:45.649
But...

14:47.120 --> 14:49.611
Most likely, Hijikata's been defeated.

14:50.790 --> 14:55.557
Still, I know he's still alive,
so long as there's a battlefield...

14:55.728 --> 14:56.820
But still...

14:57.764 --> 15:03.794
Since you've hurt your leg so badly,
I guess I can't go after Hijikata.

15:05.038 --> 15:06.733
It's all my fault...

15:07.373 --> 15:09.933
Hijikata, I'll find a way to reach you.

15:10.443 --> 15:15.107
So until I get there, stay alive!

15:18.218 --> 15:20.743
Following the Battle of Bonari...

15:21.154 --> 15:24.521
Hijikata joined Admiral Takeaki
Enomoto...

15:24.757 --> 15:27.123
...and others still loyal
to the former Shogun...

15:27.227 --> 15:28.361
<i>Daibayama, Futamagtaguchi</i>
<i> </i>

15:28.361 --> 15:30.630
<i>Daibayama, Futamagtaguchi</i>
...in the northern lands...

15:30.630 --> 15:30.930
<i>Daibayama, Futamagtaguchi</i>
<i> </i>

15:30.930 --> 15:33.666
<i>Daibayama, Futamagtaguchi</i>
...and is fighting on the island of Ezo.

15:33.666 --> 15:34.155
<i>Daibayama, Futamagtaguchi</i>
<i> </i>

15:35.802 --> 15:36.700
Get out of here!

15:36.836 --> 15:39.134
You goddamned Meiji dogs!

15:39.405 --> 15:42.033
Assassin Unit! Charge!

15:45.845 --> 15:48.473
Deputy Commander Hijikata!
A message for you!

15:50.149 --> 15:50.774
What is it?

15:51.217 --> 15:55.119
President Enomoto has ordered you
to retreat at once from Daibayama...

15:55.288 --> 15:58.746
...you are to go to the defense
of the fortress at Goryo-kaku!

15:59.993 --> 16:01.187
Retreat, he says?

16:01.327 --> 16:02.191
Yes, sir.

16:02.695 --> 16:04.356
We're winning this battle.

16:04.597 --> 16:07.225
Tell Headquarters not
to be such a killjoy!

16:07.867 --> 16:11.530
But sir, since we lost
Kikonai on the 22nd...

16:11.871 --> 16:14.704
...and Matsumae Castle on the 17th...

16:15.341 --> 16:16.968
Well, this bastion won't fall!

16:17.277 --> 16:19.040
If nothing else, the "Makoto" banner...

16:19.178 --> 16:21.169
...at Daibayama Futamataguchi
will never be taken!

16:21.648 --> 16:22.876
Still, sir...

16:23.016 --> 16:27.646
The Imperial Navy has begun a
direct assault on Hakodate Harbor...

16:27.820 --> 16:31.153
...and if Goryo-kaku were to fall,
a victory here would mean nothing...

16:31.858 --> 16:32.847
Commander Hijikata!

16:32.959 --> 16:33.891
Very well!

16:34.460 --> 16:35.392
Damn!

16:35.662 --> 16:37.789
Going north...

16:37.997 --> 16:41.865
Now that we're here in Ezo, just when
victory is finally within my reach...

16:43.236 --> 16:47.696
But if I'm the only one winning,
I suppose it's futile anyway...

16:48.207 --> 16:51.574
It looks like there won't be any
battlefields left for me soon...

16:52.645 --> 16:56.274
For some reason, there's still
something nagging at me inside...

16:56.516 --> 16:59.610
Don't you think you've
had enough, Toshizo?

16:59.719 --> 17:02.654
<i>May 11, Goryo-kaku</i>

17:02.889 --> 17:03.981
Barricade?

17:04.357 --> 17:07.656
That's right. We'd like to
hear your views, Hijikata.

17:08.094 --> 17:10.927
Who the hell's going to
send us reinforcements?

17:11.164 --> 17:14.691
Barricading is a strategy
that depends on reinforcements!

17:15.368 --> 17:18.132
No barricade has ever been
successful without reinforcements.

17:18.604 --> 17:21.903
Nevertheless, our navy
has already been crushed.

17:22.108 --> 17:25.475
And now that the Imperial
forces have occupied Hakodate...

17:25.578 --> 17:28.069
Don't get me wrong, I'm
not saying not to do it.

17:29.349 --> 17:30.543
Hijikata...

17:31.718 --> 17:36.178
Lord Enomoto, you are the
leader of the new Ezo Republic.

17:36.289 --> 17:38.018
The decision is yours to make.

17:38.491 --> 17:40.516
However, if this is our last stand...

17:41.928 --> 17:43.691
Surrender, eh?

17:43.896 --> 17:46.490
That's what you're really
contemplating, aren't you?

17:47.033 --> 17:50.560
...then I shall do as I
please with the Shinsengumi.

17:51.404 --> 17:53.463
To survive after coming this far...

17:53.639 --> 17:56.938
...how can I face Kondo and Okita,
who wait for me in the next world?

17:57.944 --> 18:00.412
Hijikata, what do you mean by that?

18:01.047 --> 18:02.071
Nothing!

18:02.248 --> 18:04.876
I'm just saying, you
should feel free to live on.

18:05.151 --> 18:06.584
I'm not saying that's wrong.

18:06.719 --> 18:08.380
Your way is just different than mine.

18:08.855 --> 18:11.119
Then what do you intend to do now?

18:11.257 --> 18:13.384
You're always going on and
on about the Shinsengumi...

18:13.493 --> 18:15.290
...but there are only
a few survivors left.

18:15.461 --> 18:18.362
At this point, the Shinsengumi as
a unit no longer exists, anywhere!

18:21.601 --> 18:23.796
I am the Shinsengumi!

18:26.606 --> 18:27.630
Now if you'll excuse me...

18:27.807 --> 18:29.707
Where do you think
you're going, Hijikata?

18:29.842 --> 18:31.707
We're in the middle
of a war council here!

18:31.944 --> 18:33.468
To change my clothes.

18:33.579 --> 18:36.480
You should know where
I'm headed after that...

18:39.118 --> 18:41.484
"I am the Shinsengumi," eh?

18:41.587 --> 18:44.647
I know I said it myself, but
now I feel so damned hopeless...

18:46.225 --> 18:47.817
You were right, Enomoto.

18:47.960 --> 18:49.825
It's just as you said.

18:50.296 --> 18:53.629
The Shinsengumi met
its end a long time ago.

18:54.333 --> 18:56.858
When Kondo surrendered
himself at Nagareyama...

18:56.969 --> 18:59.096
...that was the end of the Shinsengumi.

18:59.539 --> 19:02.030
Along with all my dreams...

19:02.442 --> 19:04.808
I can't really blame Enomoto.

19:04.911 --> 19:07.607
Though to say I'm "seeking a battle"
does have a nice ring to it...

19:08.714 --> 19:10.204
It's really no big deal.

19:10.416 --> 19:12.281
All I've done is survive until now.

19:12.452 --> 19:14.386
If my intention was to die
as a Shinsengumi member...

19:14.487 --> 19:16.489
...then I should've stopped Kondo
from giving himself up,

19:16.489 --> 19:17.421
no matter what...

19:17.924 --> 19:20.358
...and then we could have met the
Imperial forces together...

19:20.460 --> 19:22.826
...as the Shinsengumi, we
should've died in battle!

19:23.062 --> 19:26.395
And yet, why is it that I
have lived to see this day?

19:26.699 --> 19:30.533
To seek revenge for our defeat
at the Battle of Toba-Fushimi?

19:31.871 --> 19:33.395
Strange, isn't it...

19:33.606 --> 19:37.098
It's no longer the age of the sword, even
though I'd recognized it at the time...

19:37.610 --> 19:40.773
...and switched to Western battle
tactics, cut off my topknot...

19:40.913 --> 19:45.407
...and put on Western-style clothes,
I still can't give up my sword!

19:45.785 --> 19:47.343
"How should I kill him?"

19:47.453 --> 19:50.115
There's a part of me that
still ponders that question.

19:51.958 --> 19:54.188
"How should I kill that man?"

19:54.694 --> 19:55.888
Wait!

19:56.796 --> 19:58.354
It's him, isn't it?

20:02.101 --> 20:06.538
Though I've fought and fought, until
I finally felt that I'd had enough...

20:06.706 --> 20:09.140
...there was still
something nagging at me...

20:09.442 --> 20:12.775
I was waiting for that man, wasn't I?

20:14.113 --> 20:18.140
Somewhere deep inside,
I knew he'd be coming to see me...

20:18.885 --> 20:20.978
...that's the feeling I think I had...

20:21.087 --> 20:23.214
...no, I'm sure I had it!

20:23.322 --> 20:27.088
Unfortunately, I guess that
was just another dream of mine!

20:31.197 --> 20:32.528
Now, then...

20:33.366 --> 20:34.492
Shall I go?

20:35.167 --> 20:37.032
All the way to hell...

20:37.637 --> 20:39.969
My horse! Bring my horse!

20:41.307 --> 20:42.569
Hijikata!

20:44.010 --> 20:46.444
Hijikata, where are you going?

20:46.979 --> 20:48.412
Why are you dressed like that?

20:48.514 --> 20:50.539
Surely you're not going to attack?

20:50.883 --> 20:52.407
The council has decided on a
barricade...

20:52.885 --> 20:54.011
Hijikata!

20:54.320 --> 20:56.379
I'm on my way to hell, men!

20:57.857 --> 21:00.621
Then we will go with you!

21:01.260 --> 21:02.852
Take us with you, please!

21:03.930 --> 21:06.990
Idiot! Life is something
to be cherished.

21:07.099 --> 21:09.329
Even if you follow me, I'll
be sure to leave you behind!

21:10.736 --> 21:11.794
Open the gate!

21:18.611 --> 21:20.636
<i>To be continued...</i>

21:31.824 --> 21:43.861
<i>Those summer stars, I looked up at</i>
<i>them alone when I was a troubled child.</i>

21:44.136 --> 21:53.875
<i>My loneliness and the vast night</i>
<i>sky, melting and shining in eternity.</i>

21:54.013 --> 22:03.012
<i>I just don't know what this</i>
<i>dream means, if it leads to love...</i>

22:03.155 --> 22:13.827
<i>Even if it's just "hello,"</i>
<i>I want to hear your voice.</i>

22:14.867 --> 22:20.999
<i>The person I am today</i>
<i>is about to disappear...</i>

22:21.374 --> 22:24.400
<i>What is it that will hold me back?</i>

22:25.244 --> 22:31.513
<i>Will it be you? I won't ask you now.</i>

22:31.817 --> 22:37.312
<i>Maybe if we ever meet again...</i>

22:52.038 --> 22:55.269
You're just made of murderous
intent, aren't you, Hijikata?

22:55.841 --> 22:58.639
Now then, let's do it!

22:59.645 --> 23:02.113
Final episode of the Age of Chaos...

23:02.248 --> 23:03.681
The Demon and the Shura

23:03.783 --> 23:06.081
Pay close attention, and wait!
